{"total_count":975,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/58809","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/58809/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/58809/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/58809/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/58809","id":6156082719,"node_id":"I_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAABbu5eHw","number":58809,"title":"macOS: browser access silently stops mid-chat; approval changes never re-prompt, Work toggle restores access","user":{"login":"RicardoMiles","id":150692986,"node_id":"U_kgDOCPtkeg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/150692986?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RicardoMiles","html_url":"https://github.com/RicardoMiles","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RicardoMiles/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RicardoMiles/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RicardoMiles/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RicardoMiles/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RicardoMiles/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RicardoMiles/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RicardoMiles/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RicardoMiles/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RicardoMiles/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":8448146916,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAAB94x95A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":10121036495,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAACW0LCzw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/labels/app","name":"app","color":"401e87","default":false,"description":"Issues related to the Codex desktop app","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":10853139785,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAAChuXFSQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/labels/browser","name":"browser","color":"828f71","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-11-02T04:17:02Z","updated_at":"2026-11-02T04:56:05Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### What version of the Codex App are you using (From “About Codex” dialog)?\n\nThe incident desktop logs report `release=26.1023.51421`. The About-dialog version was not captured at the time; I am identifying this as the log release value rather than substituting today's installed version.\n\n### What subscription do you have?\n\nNot recorded in the incident evidence.\n\n### What platform is your computer?\n\nmacOS host, controlling an existing Google Chrome session through Codex browser tools. Part of the later troubleshooting was conducted from a phone through the remote chat. The incident OS build was not captured.\n\n### What issue are you seeing?\n\nBrowser access stopped during an established, explicitly authorized workflow. I had been using it successfully in the same conversation earlier that evening. I had selected **Full access**, never manually turned off local browser use, and saw no notification that browser access or its effective authorization had changed.\n\nFull access was the UI mode I selected; the effective browser authorization for each failed turn was not independently captured.\n\nAfter the failure, I switched to **Approve for me** and then **Ask for approval** to try to get an authorization prompt back. Neither gave me a new prompt or a usable recovery path. New conversations were also affected.\n\nThe initial tool errors pointed to a declined action and then a saved website-permission block. The website permission UI showed allowance, and the Chrome extension had access to all sites. Troubleshooting consequently kept focusing on website authorization and a saved conversation-level denial.\n\nOnly later did a fresh conversation report:\n\n```text\nLocal browser use is disabled in Work settings\n```\n\nI eventually recovered browser access by setting:\n\n**Settings → Work preferences → Local browser use → On**\n\nI can confirm that recovery action. I cannot identify when or why the effective Work browser permission changed. There is no captured setting-write event establishing an On → Off transition or its source.\n\nThe problem I want investigated is the complete transition and recovery experience: a working browser became unavailable without an action from me, the failure was initially presented as website authorization, and changing the approval mode did not let me authorize it again. Finding the separate Work control took substantial troubleshooting.\n\n### What steps can reproduce the bug?\n\nThis is the recorded failure sequence, not a deterministic reproduction. The trigger is still unknown.\n\n1. Continue using browser tools in an existing conversation against an already accessible HTTPS site.\n2. Successfully read the page, interact with it, and take a screenshot.\n3. In the same conversation, a later page read fails with a permission denial.\n4. Check the extension and website permission controls; they show access allowed.\n5. Switch from Full access to Approve for me and Ask for approval. No fresh authorization prompt appears and access remains blocked.\n6. Try a new conversation. Browser inventory reports that local browser use is disabled in Work settings.\n7. Find the separate Work preferences control and set Local browser use to On. Browser access recovers.\n\n#### Timestamped tool evidence\n\nAll times below are UTC, which was also UK local time on these dates. These are recorded tool-result timestamps, not measured setting-change times.\n\n| Time | Observation |\n| --- | --- |\n| 2026-10-29 23:42:37.778 | Power BI report DOM read succeeded in the original conversation. |\n| 2026-10-29 23:42:55.433 | Report screenshot was captured and saved successfully. |\n| 2026-10-29 23:53:45.468 | A later DOM read in the same conversation failed: `Browser Use rejected this action due to browser security policy. Reason: The user declined permission for this action.` The result also said the origin approval gate did not grant access. |\n| 2026-10-30 00:15:57.964 | Another attempt failed with `A saved user permission setting blocks this action.` |\n| 2026-10-30 01:45:15.994 | Browser inventory in a new conversation returned `Local browser use is disabled in Work settings`. |\n| 2026-10-30 01:47:36.949 and 02:02:54.162 | The troubleshooting conversation returned the same Work-disabled error on repeated inventory requests. |\n\nThe last successful screenshot and first recorded origin denial are about **10 minutes 50 seconds apart**. That bounds an observed access regression; it does not establish when the Work preference changed.\n\nRead-only inspection also found the affected site under `origins.denied` in the original conversation's browser session policy. That establishes a saved denial existed, not who created it. Likewise, the tool text “The user declined” is not evidence that I clicked a denial prompt.\n\n### What is the expected behavior?\n\nI understand that Full access does not override every browser-specific control. But the product needs to make the actual authorization state understandable and recoverable.\n\n- **Explain the effective block.** Distinguish a disabled Work capability, a saved site denial, a managed restriction, and a runtime/session authorization failure. Point to the actual control that applies.\n- **Make a capability change visible.** When browser access becomes unavailable during active work, surface what changed and why. If the app cannot establish the cause, do not attribute it to a user denial without evidence.\n- **Provide reauthorization in the affected chat.** Give me a supported way to review/reset a saved denial and request authorization again while preserving my task and browser session. Switching to Ask for approval did not provide that path here.\n- **Make recovery verifiable.** After changing the relevant setting, let the user retry the failed capability and see its effective status.\n\n### Additional information\n\nThe evidence contains two different refusal classes: an origin-permission denial, followed later by a Work browser-access denial in a new conversation. They may be related, but I have not established one root cause for both.\n\nOne tempting log interpretation has already been ruled out: at 01:33:58.007 the desktop log briefly reported `browserPane=false` / `available=false`, then reported both true **56 ms later**. That transient is not evidence that the Work setting was persistently disabled.\n\nPlease correlate the successful → denied window with Work preference values/revisions and write sources, the decision that persisted the origin denial, and runtime/session authorization decisions. The local evidence reviewed so far does not contain an authoritative setting-change audit trail.\n\nRelated reports:\n\n- #54989 — same Work-disabled error; an October 24 follow-up recovered by enabling the separate Work Local browser use control.\n- #57721 — mobile-created remote conversations receive a misleading Work-disabled error despite the setting being enabled.\n- #56734 — website permission allowance and a persisted conversation-level origin denial disagree.\n\nThis report adds a timestamped **working → denied transition in the same conversation**, the failed approval-mode recovery attempts, cross-conversation impact, and the eventual Work-toggle recovery. It does not claim the related reports have the same cause.\n\nPrivate report/model identifiers, account identifiers, local personal paths, raw transcripts, screenshots, credentials, and business data are omitted. No permission files or installed application code were modified during this investigation.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/58809/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/58809/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai","html_url":"https://github.com/openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"ChatGPT Codex Connector","description":"Bring ChatGPT and Codex to your GitHub repositories.","external_url":"https://www.chatgpt.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector","created_at":"2025-02-14T01:37:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T18:52:59Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","checks":"read","contents":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","issues","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","repository","status","sub_issues"]},"state_reason":"reopened","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/58439","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/58439/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/58439/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/58439/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/58439","id":6127478369,"node_id":"I_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAABbTnmYQ","number":58439,"title":"Desktop browser origin remains denied for a chat after website permission is explicitly allowed","user":{"login":"LIBREYLOCO","id":254318576,"node_id":"U_kgDODyiX8A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254318576?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LIBREYLOCO","html_url":"https://github.com/LIBREYLOCO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LIBREYLOCO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LIBREYLOCO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LIBREYLOCO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LIBREYLOCO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LIBREYLOCO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LIBREYLOCO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LIBREYLOCO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LIBREYLOCO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LIBREYLOCO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":8448146916,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAAB94x95A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":10121036495,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAACW0LCzw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/labels/app","name":"app","color":"401e87","default":false,"description":"Issues related to the Codex desktop app","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":10853139785,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAAChuXFSQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/labels/browser","name":"browser","color":"828f71","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-10-30T21:48:52Z","updated_at":"2026-11-02T04:56:01Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Environment\n- macOS desktop app version 26.1023.51421, build22530.\n- Browser Use through built-in browser and Chrome extension.\n\nReproduction\n1. A website origin was previously denied in an existing chat.\n2. User explicitly changes Settings > Browser > website navigation permission to Always allow for the exact origin.\n3. Read-only diagnostics show the origin allowed in ~/.codex/config.toml and ~/.codex/browser/config.toml, while ~/.codex/browser/sessions/<chat-id>.toml still contains the same origin in origins.denied.\n4. Retrying Browser Use in that chat returns: “A saved user permission setting blocks this action” and “The origin approval gate did not grant access”. No new approval prompt appears.\n5. Removing the site exception to restore Requires approval and retrying did not produce a new approval prompt. Resetting the browser REPL did not resolve it. Both built-in browser and Chrome requests are rejected before navigation.\n\nExpected\nAn explicit user permission change should provide a supported way to revoke a chat-specific denial, or the UI should clearly expose the overriding session decision and offer reauthorization.\n\nActual\nVisible website permissions and stored global allow rules disagree with the chat-scoped denial. The user cannot complete authorized desktop/mobile QA of their website.\n\nDiagnosis scope\nThe files confirm conflicting global and session permissions. This suggests precedence or invalidation behavior, but the exact application-level cause has not been established. No permission files were modified, no policy bypass attempted. No credentials, customer data, chat ID, or raw transcripts are included.\n\nRequest\nPlease document a supported session-denial reset or fix invalidation of stale per-chat origin decisions when the user explicitly changes website permissions.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/58439/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/58439/timeline","performed_via_github_app":{"id":1144995,"client_id":"Iv23liVemv8A9if9v0F2","slug":"chatgpt-codex-connector","node_id":"A_kwHOAOQ6Gs4AEXij","owner":{"login":"openai","id":14957082,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjE0OTU3MDgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14957082?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai","html_url":"https://github.com/openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/openai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"ChatGPT Codex Connector","description":"Bring ChatGPT and Codex to your GitHub repositories.","external_url":"https://www.chatgpt.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/chatgpt-codex-connector","created_at":"2025-02-14T01:37:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T18:52:59Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","checks":"read","contents":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","commit_comment","issues","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","repository","status","sub_issues"]},"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}